@urbanayanvlogs people don’t give fuck about their safety. Just look at bike riders in Pakistan. They only wear helmets because of 2000 ka challan. Agr in ko itni fikr hoti to khd ki safety k pye pehenty na k fines k lye. Or khd k sth pechy bethy bandy ko b pehenaty. Lekin nahi. 
Agr safety dekhy awam to yh Alto or yh jo teen dabby civic ya koi suzuki ki gari jis m [PLATE REDACTED] airbag b mushkil sy aty h wo kbhi b na bikfi Pakistan m.  
Puri duniya m is civic m 11 airbags hoty h or apny Pakistan m [PLATE REDACTED] or is teen dabby ko ly k Pakistani awam itni shokhi hoti h 😂 afsoos hota hai inki jahalat py. Inko jo b becho ly lety h bechary

@Bruhwhat99 
Yes,but! We never cared and nothing mayor never happened and we used our breaks to the last drop of metal. Now the garage is different, they have to follow safety protocols or shut down because of law suits. I was very careful with my work car, but the spare one just used and abused and barely repaired when not just mending it as you go. Yes I agree with everything here, but they haven't explained the consequences of using bad breaks according to them but that still works fine according to us. 
If you keep your bearings in good shape the breaks should last longer than usual. I would usually change my bearings every so often depending on workshop manual recommendations. Only then I would overhaul the breaks, but for the rest of the time just new pads on and keep going.

